From 1b5f11b81a3bd68a74a59a21d6a5a0c00f991c89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Mar 2026 18:39:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 277/913] drivers: stm32_iwdg: use DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM()

Replace DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER() directive with DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM()
for resources that need to be unpaged for PM sequence support for
stm32mp15 platforms.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a8c2d86c1991737071e86ee677349d96d45fabd4 drivers: stm32_iwdg: use DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM()]
Signed-off-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I370b2ba1ab85bb34ed1b6839aa702eca6fa1f96b
---
 core/drivers/stm32_iwdg.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_iwdg.c b/core/drivers/stm32_iwdg.c
index bf2eba4e1..032436fc3 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_iwdg.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_iwdg.c
@@ -539,7 +539,7 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_iwdg_pm(enum pm_op op, unsigned int pm_hint __unused,
 
 	return TEE_SUCCESS;
 }
-DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER(stm32_iwdg_pm);
+DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM(stm32_iwdg_pm);
 
 static TEE_Result stm32_iwdg_probe(const void *fdt, int node,
 				   const void *compat_data __unused)
-- 
2.53.0

